    summary: "The Journal of Breast Imaging is the official journal of the Society of Breast Imaging, published by Oxford University Press and catalogued by NLM from 2019 under the subject headings Breast Diseases and Early Detection of Cancer. Its about page describes it as a peer-reviewed publication that aims to provide high quality, evidence-based content for the global breast imaging medical community, with a focus on improving patient care across screening, diagnosis, image-guided procedures and cancer management. It publishes original research together with reviews of important scientific, educational and clinical topics. The publisher page indicates a subscription model with open access options for individual articles, so the access model is recorded here as hybrid.",
