    tldr: "The open access journal for wasting syndromes: the muscle and weight loss that accompanies advanced cancer and other chronic diseases. Read by oncologists, geriatricians, nutrition scientists and muscle biologists.",
    summary: "The Journal of Cachexia, Sarcopenia and Muscle is published by Wiley on behalf of the Society on Sarcopenia, Cachexia and Wasting Disorders, which describes it as a peer-reviewed international journal dedicated to publishing both research and clinical materials related to cachexia and sarcopenia from all fields of the life sciences. NLM catalogues it from 2010 as a quarterly, first published in Germany, indexed for MEDLINE under Cachexia, Muscles and Sarcopenia. The Directory of Open Access Journals lists it as fully open access since 2010 under a CC BY licence, with anonymous peer review and an article processing charge.",
