    tldr: "The official journal of the International Society of Oncology Pharmacy Practitioners, covering how cancer medicines are prepared, dosed, handled and used safely. Read by oncology pharmacists and pharmacy technicians.",
    summary: "Journal of Oncology Pharmacy Practice (JOPP) is published by SAGE Publications and is the official publication of the International Society of Oncology Pharmacy Practitioners (ISOPP). ISOPP describes it as a peer-reviewed, scholarly journal dedicated to educating health professionals about providing pharmaceutical care to patients with cancer. It publishes original research, reviews and practice-issues papers, including comprehensive and critical reviews of drug use in cancer care, institutional medication-use policies with outcome indicators, reports of innovative services and outcome measurement tools, opinions on controversial therapeutic areas, and updates on ISOPP activities. The journal is a member of the Committee on Publication Ethics and is free to ISOPP members. NLM records it as starting in 1995, published in London, and currently indexed in MEDLINE.",
