    summary: "Journal of Pediatric Hematology/Oncology is published by Lippincott Williams & Wilkins, part of Wolters Kluwer, and is hosted on the Ovid journals platform. The journal page lists eight issues a year under Editor-in-Chief Bruce M. Camitta and carries clinical papers on childhood blood disorders and cancers; recent issue highlights include a case report on immunotherapy for constitutional mismatch repair deficiency-associated bowel adenocarcinoma in a child, and a retrospective cohort study of vaccine immunity to measles, mumps, rubella and varicella in childhood leukaemia survivors after chemotherapy. NLM records the journal as starting in 1995 (print ISSN 1077-4114, electronic ISSN 1536-3678), published in Hagerstown, Maryland, and currently indexed in MEDLINE.",
