    summary: "Journal of Psychosocial Oncology is published by Routledge, part of Taylor & Francis, and is affiliated with the Association of Oncology Social Work. The publisher describes it as a single source of integrated information on providing the best psychosocial care possible, drawing on knowledge from many disciplines and emphasising an interdisciplinary approach to care and research in oncology, and as an essential source of up-to-date clinical and research material for health professionals who provide psychosocial services to cancer patients, their families and caregivers. It is an Open Select (hybrid) journal, so authors may choose to publish open access while other content is available by subscription. NLM records the journal as starting in 1983, published in Philadelphia, and currently indexed in MEDLINE.",
