    tldr: "A long-running surgical journal for cancer surgeons, covering operations, multimodality treatment and the laboratory science behind them, with themed Seminars issues.",
    summary: "Journal of Surgical Oncology is published by Wiley (copyright Wiley Periodicals) and edited by David J. Bentrem. The journal states that it publishes research in the field of surgical and clinical oncology and broadly related surgical sciences, including experimental and laboratory studies on cancer research and treatment, pathology, radiology, multimodality treatment and more, and that it encourages participation from leading surgeons and cancer specialists around the world. Guest editors from the editorial board oversee several special Seminars issues each year, including congress proceedings such as those of the Brazilian Congress of Surgical Oncology. The journal offers an open access publishing route alongside its subscription content and warns authors about an unrelated journal using a similar name. NLM records it as starting in 1969, published in Hoboken, New Jersey, and currently indexed in MEDLINE.",
    links: [{ label: "Homepage", url: "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10969098" }, { label: "NLM Catalog", url: "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nlmcatalog/222643" }],
